---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page
  title="Privacy"
  kicker="Legal"
  description="What this site collects, why, and how to opt out — analytics, the contact form, and third-party services."
  wide={false}
>
  <div class="prose-nw">
    <p class="text-faint"><em>Last updated: 28 July 2026</em></p>

    <p>
      This is a personal portfolio site. It sells nothing, has no accounts, and collects as little
      as it can get away with.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      The site uses Google Analytics 4 in <strong>cookieless</strong> mode. No <code>_ga</code> cookies
      are written, nothing is stored in your browser between visits, and IP addresses are anonymised before
      processing. What is recorded is aggregate: which pages get read, roughly where traffic comes from,
      and which links referred it. There is no way for me to tie any of that back to you, and no returning-visitor
      tracking.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you would rather send nothing at all, any content or tracker blocker will stop the
      requests, as will your browser's "Do Not Track" or equivalent setting in blockers that honour
      it.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact form</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> is handled by
      <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy">Formspree</a>. Whatever you type into it —
      your name, email address, and message — is transmitted to Formspree and forwarded to my inbox.
      It is used to reply to you and nothing else: no mailing list, no sharing, no resale. You can
      email me directly at <a href="mailto:noah@noahweidig.com">noah@noahweidig.com</a> instead if you
      would rather skip the intermediary.
    </p>

    <h2>Scheduling</h2>
    <p>
      The "Book a Call" links go to <a href="https://cal.com/privacy">Cal.com</a>, which handles its
      own booking data under its own privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting and fonts</h2>
    <p>
      The site is static, served by GitHub Pages, with deploy previews on Netlify. Both keep
      standard server request logs, which I do not have access to. Fonts are self-hosted, so no font
      CDN sees your visit.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      If you are in the EU, UK, or another jurisdiction with data protection law and want to know
      what I hold about you, or want it deleted, email
      <a href="mailto:noah@noahweidig.com">noah@noahweidig.com</a>. In practice the only thing that
      ever exists is a message you sent me yourself.
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>
